      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-35791",
      ":question/problem": "There are three groups of fans in a certain town: those who prefer basketball, those who prefer baseball, and those who prefer football. A study has shown that, each year\n\n- from the people that prefer basketball, $32%$ change to baseball and $28%$ change to football,\n- from the people that prefer baseball, $45%$ change to football and $15%$ change to basketball,\n- from the people that prefer football, $25%$ change to basketball and $65%$ change to baseball.\n\nThe stochastic matrix that describes this situation is given below. What is the value of $a + b + c$?\n\n$P = \\begin{bmatrix}0.4 & 0.15 & a \\\\ 0.32 & b & 0.65 \\\\ c & 0.45 & 0.1\\end{bmatrix}$"
